  "summary": "Senior Software Engineer | Lead Architect | Secret Clearance | DOD 8570.01-M (IAT II)\n\nHigh-impact architect specializing in the modernization of mission-critical defense systems. I provide a rare combination of Enterprise ICAM Architecture, Zero Trust implementation, and full-lifecycle RMF/ATO ownership.\n\nI don't just write code; I design the security-first frameworks that protect government data and mission-critical revenue.\n\nThe Impact:\n\nIdentity & Access Management (ICAM): Serving as the sole architect for a cross-service role-provisioning platform integrated across two Armed Services. Currently spearheading the transition to a Zero Trust architecture, replacing legacy enterprise suites valued at $20M+ in annual revenue.\n\nCloud Modernization: Orchestrated the organization’s first successful synchronous-to-async Azure cloud migration. Spearheaded the complete rewrite of legacy .NET Framework applications to .NET Core, establishing the blueprint for future enterprise cloud strategy.\n\nCompliance & Authorization: 100% accountability for the RMF lifecycle, including the creation and management of all PO&Ms and DISA/MCCOG coordination. I bridge the gap between complex engineering and the Authority to Operate (ATO).\n\nTechnical Governance: Primary technical liaison for all levels of government stakeholders. I provide real-time architectural justification and roadmap governance in multi-agency briefings to ensure mission alignment.",
